00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:38.613
Unusual Wales walks through a screen that asks whether a name beat on both revenue and

00:01:38.613 --> 00:01:43.713
operating margin and whether that margin gain came from volume rather than a one-time item.

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:48.833
On wealth simple or quest trade and I have no financial relationship with either platform,

00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:53.933
form. You can pull the last four quarters, line actual results against the same day consensus,

00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:59.533
and finish the comparison in under five minutes. Open the earnings release PDF from the company

00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:04.913
site, find the revenue line and the operating margin line, and subtract the consensus figure

00:02:04.913 --> 00:02:10.413
published that morning by the major data providers. The name passes the first filter only if both

00:02:10.413 --> 00:02:15.993
lines clear those estimates and the commentary credits higher throughput volumes, not an asset

00:02:15.993 --> 00:02:21.653
sale or some other one off. The second filter is the sector exchange traded fund, or ETF,

00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:28.013
over the prior five sessions. If that ETF is down more than 2% while the single name is flat

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:33.153
or up, rotation risk is elevated and the position should be cut in half before you size it.

00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:40.433
Historical back tests on TSX Energy Names from 2022 to 2025 showed this two-step filter

00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:46.353
produce positive alpha in 58% of cases when announcement day volume exceeded the 20-day

00:02:46.353 --> 00:02:46.733
average.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:51.833
That edge disappeared when volume lagged, which is why the volume check is not optional

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:52.193
color.

00:02:52.753 --> 00:02:57.213
The window is the first 48 hours after the release, before the rest of the tape finishes

00:02:57.213 --> 00:02:58.093
pricing the print.

00:02:58.753 --> 00:03:03.033
Hotter than forecast producer prices are the macro reason this screen matters today.

00:03:03.633 --> 00:03:09.593
Upstream costs feed company margins first, then consumer prices later, and downstream operators

00:03:09.593 --> 00:03:12.413
get squeezed unless they can pass those costs through.

00:03:13.013 --> 00:03:15.653
Enbridge's most recent quarter is the worked example.

