00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:02.640
Under published rules, fixed $1,000 size, entry at the next open, five session holds, stopper

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:08.440
horizon exits, no discretionary closes. Because that alpha figure compounds 28 independent

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:13.300
matched windows rather than a single buy and hold, it isolates the selection and timing

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:18.680
rules. You reproduce it by recording the NASDAQ on each entry day and each exit day and

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:24.657
compounding those returns over the same interval. You bought a name after an earnings beat, parked

00:09:24.657 --> 00:09:30.377
a mental stop 5% below the entry, and then watched it drift on sector rotation. The drop

00:09:30.377 --> 00:09:35.837
feels temporary so you hesitate, and that hesitation is hindsight rationalization. The

00:09:35.837 --> 00:09:39.457
thesis keeps getting edited because you never wrote the thing that would prove it wrong.

00:09:40.097 --> 00:09:45.157
A round number stop is not protection. It is a price that can always be called too tight after

00:09:45.157 --> 00:09:50.457
the fact. The fix is to write an observable falsification trigger on the same note as the entry

00:09:50.457 --> 00:09:56.257
price and the catalyst, before any capital is committed. First sentence of that note is the thesis

00:09:56.257 --> 00:10:02.237
in one line. Volume growth on the system will sustain distribution coverage above 1.2 times.

00:10:02.817 --> 00:10:08.057
Second sentence is the observable that kills it, tied to a dated release rather than to the tape.

00:10:08.617 --> 00:10:13.497
Third, the stop is calculated backward from that coverage number using the current payout ratio

00:10:13.497 --> 00:10:19.077
and the expected free cash flow range, so the exit is a translation of the original idea.

00:10:19.597 --> 00:10:24.877
Because the trigger sits on a known calendar date, you cannot later claim the stop was too tight or too

00:10:24.877 --> 00:10:28.377
loose, the data either confirmed the sentence or refuted it.

00:10:28.777 --> 00:10:33.677
That is also what blocks the common error of widening the stop after entry, because editing

00:10:33.677 --> 00:10:37.957
the invalidation means rewriting the thesis, not massaging a percentage.

00:10:38.557 --> 00:10:42.437
Over a string of tickets you log, which invalidations fired, and which did not.

00:10:42.917 --> 00:10:45.697
And that log tells you whether the screen itself needs work.

00:10:46.257 --> 00:10:51.217
Rule, write the observable falsification trigger on the same note as the entry before capital

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:54.597
is committed, and do not edit it without rewriting the thesis.

00:10:55.712 --> 00:11:00.412
Open your TFS holdings list, find the single largest position, and write down the exact

00:11:00.412 --> 00:11:05.052
coverage ratio or earning surprise number that would force you to reconsider it.

